Banana OS - AMD Radeon TeraScale 2 display driver: third-party notices
==========================================================================

third_party/radeon/ holds, from Linux's drivers/gpu/drm/radeon (v6.12):
  atom.c, atom.h, atom-bits.h, atom-names.h   the AtomBIOS interpreter
                                               (Copyright 2008 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.;
                                               author Stanislaw Skowronek)
  atombios.h, atom-types.h, ObjectID.h,       AMD's AtomBIOS table definitions
  pptable.h, radeon_family.h                  (Copyright 2006-2013 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.)
Changes for Banana OS: linux_compat.h stands in for the Linux kernel's
headers; every read of the BIOS image is bounded by its size (atom-bits.h);
atom_parse takes the image's size; the card's family comes from card_info.

evergreen_wm.c holds evergreen.c's display watermark arithmetic (Copyright
2010 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.), the priority mark computed in 64 bits.
radeon_cs_check.c holds the command-stream checker of evergreen_cs.c,
r600_cs.c (formats table) and radeon_cs.c (packet parsing, relocations),
Copyright 2008-2010 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc., Red Hat Inc., Jerome
Glisse; radeon_cs_shim.h stands in for the driver's structures.
evergreen_reg_safe.h / cayman_reg_safe.h are generated by
tools/radeon_regtable.py from reg_srcs/ (Linux's register lists);
radeon_drm.h is Linux's uapi header (MIT, Copyright 2000 Precision Insight,
VA Linux Systems, 2002 Tungsten Graphics).

kernel/radeon_atom.c and kernel/radeon_kms.c follow Linux's radeon_bios.c,
radeon_device.c, radeon_atombios.c, atombios_i2c.c, atombios_crtc.c,
atombios_encoders.c, radeon_display.c and evergreen.c (Copyright 2007-2008
